tantra3 sparsha

-- sparsha: true contact.
--
-- sparsha (Sanskrit) = touch, contact, the moment of meeting.
-- in vedanta: the second of the five sense-contacts (tanmatra).
-- here: the moment the sentence touches the proof graph.
-- dhvani (surface sound) becomes artha (structural meaning).
--
-- sparsha is NOT compression. it is expansion.
-- the sentence, which is a linear sequence of phonemes,
-- is expanded into a typed directed multigraph.
-- every word lands as either:
--   satya  — known, reflexive, structurally confirmed
--   mithya — provisional, held, not yet grounded
--
-- the distinction is everything.
-- satya words already exist in the brahman (kosha + sangati).
-- mithya words are not failures — they are avidya: not-yet-known.
-- context pressure (avrti) will collapse mithya into satya.
-- what remains mithya after fixpoint is genuine asprista:
-- a word with no grounding even in full domain context.
--
-- sparsha calls build-question-graph.
-- build-question-graph calls:
--   sandhi-viveka    — grammar promotion (has→shashthi, was→bhuta-kaala)
--   emit-triples     — word → satya/mithya/asprista-sankhya/matra/vidhi-kaala
--   find-context     — tracks active-concept, pending-number
--
-- sparsha receives the sentence. returns the raw contact graph.
-- avrti has not yet run. mithya is still mithya.
-- this is the moment before understanding. understanding begins now.

takes sentence

result = build-question-graph sentence

return result

done
